Z||000000||GT Bastard||11-05-2000||02:05 PM||||So a friend and I meet this guy driving an '87 gold 2M4... Only it's not a 2.5!  It's a turbocharged 1.6 VW Diesel motor mated to a 5sp.  This thing is nuts.... The guy has this huge-assed intercooler and no muffler.  He chopped the fiero and vw axles in half, and then mated them together with a sleeve and welded it.  It gets even MORE unusual!!!  He's building an '86 SE with an ISUZU 3.2 litre motor and a twin turbo setup.  He's having a shop in Arizona build the Izuzu motor to withstand excess of 10,000 rpm.  I wouldn't have believed this guy if he didn't have a VW turbo diesel motor to proove it. Apparently, he rebuilds manual and auto trannies for a living.  He must be mid-thirties, and he was talking about smoking rice-boys.  F*cking cool!!!!  Apprently, he's using turbo's from a 1990 Talon TSi.  I'm going to get pictures soon!!!!  He apparently has a whole fleet of custom built cars(6.5 diesel Cherokee, 2-cyl motorcycle engine in a Samurai, etc....)  Anyhow, I asked him about all kinds of advice for a turbo setup on my car, and he's got plenty of ideas.  He's using a CSI mechanical fuel injection system fro a VW on his Isuzu motor.  Custom built manifold using 2 CSI units.  nuts...||||reg||4
Z||000001||stimpy||11-05-2000||03:32 PM||||Sounds kinda nuts alright. Does he want a 16 valve turbo 1.6 liter Mazda engine? Easily tuned for 180 hp? I'll get him a hell of a deal!||||reg||1
